{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1031660-adapting-adventures","id":1031660,"title":"Adapting adventures","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-14T10:24:38-08:00","id":1031660,"title":"Adapting adventures","content":"So have any of you adapted adventures from other game systems? If so which ones? and how much did you convert?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12662-bestial-warlust","name":"bestial Warlust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T18:49:54-08:00","id":1032423,"title":"","content":"I converted the first part of Nocturnum, a Call of Cthulhu adventure, for a vanilla mortals game. All I had to convert were game stats but to be honest it proved disappointing. True Chronicles of Darkness is not intended to be played as a hack &amp; slash game but compared to Cthulhu it might as well be full contact fighting, even when focusing on banes &amp; bans. Having a final confrontation that consists of the heroes all holding onto a magical McGuffin and making Stamina/Resolve rolls in the hopes that one of them will stay alive and conscious long enough for said McGuffin to banish the big bad came across as flat and anti-climatic.<br /> In Cthulhu characters are supposed to feel helpless, in CofD they should just feel greatly challenged.<br /> I had much better luck borrowing a temple from a D&amp;D module, Necropolis, for a Mage game. I just declared it to be a hidden 'Atlantian' temple with its own Spirit, passed off the occupants as manifestations generated by that Spirit and placed the players' goal in the basement crypt. The map worked great and again all I had to convert were game stats. It even had pictures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T20:42:04-08:00","id":1032463,"title":"","content":"I actually have that one. It's a big hard cover one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12662-bestial-warlust","name":"bestial Warlust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}